20 'minus' 3 + 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 12 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s1\sl466 {\*\bkmkstart ID_expressions}{\*\bkmkend ID_expressions}\b\fs35\f1 7 Expressions\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_expr_45_overview}{\*\bkmkend ID_expr_45_overview}\fs31 7.1 Overview\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Expressions are the core computational units of Scaly. Every expression evaluates to a value. An operation is a sequence of operands; operators are ordinary identifiers rather than built-in keywords. When operators are chained, they combine according to standard mathematical precedence (multiplicative binds tighter than additive, which binds tighter than comparison). Prefix forms and parentheses provide explicit control where needed.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_category_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_category_45_LITERALS}\b\fs31\lang1024\f1 7.2 Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Expressions are the core computational units of Scaly. Every expression evaluates to a value.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_BOOLEAN_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_BOOLEAN_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 7.2.1 Boolean Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 The boolean literals are true and false.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_INTEGER_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_INTEGER_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\f1 7.2.2 Integer Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Integer literals are sequences of decimal digits, optionally preceded by a minus sign for negative numbers.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -7\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -7 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_HEX_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_HEX_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\f1 7.2.3 Hexadecimal Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Hexadecimal literals start with 0x or 0X followed by hexadecimal digits (0-9, a-f, A-F).\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0xFF\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 255 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0x1A\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 26 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0x0\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_FLOAT_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_FLOAT_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\f1 7.2.4 Floating-Point Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Floating-point literals contain a decimal point separating the integer and fractional parts.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3.14\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3.14 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 2.0\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 2.0 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0.5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 0.5 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_STRING_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_STRING_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\f1 7.2.5 String Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 String literals are enclosed in double quotes. They may span multiple lines, with line breaks preserved in the resulting string.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 "hello"\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 hello \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 ""\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2  \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_CHARACTER_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_CHARACTER_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\f1 7.2.6 Character Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Character literals represent a single character, enclosed in backticks.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 `a`\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 a \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 `Z`\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 Z \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_category_45_OPERATIONS}{\*\bkmkend ID_category_45_OPERATIONS}\b\fs31\f1 7.3 Operations\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Operations allow combining expressions.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_PREFIX_45_FUNCTIONS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_PREFIX_45_FUNCTIONS}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 7.3.1 Prefix Functions\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 An operation is a sequence of operands that evaluates to a single value. Each operand is an expression optionally followed by member access. An operation ends with a colon, a line break, or anything which is not an expression. Evaluation uses a context which is empty at the start of an operation. When the context is empty, operator-shaped identifiers act as prefix functions, taking the next operand as their argument.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -7\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -7 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -(-3)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 + 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_OPERATOR_45_CHAINS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_OPERATOR_45_CHAINS}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.2 Operator Chains\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 When the context holds a value, operators combine with operands according to standard mathematical precedence. Multiplicative operators (*, /, %, div, mod) bind tighter than additive operators (+, -). Comparison and equality operators have lower precedence than arithmetic. Operators of equal precedence associate left-to-right.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 + 4\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 7 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 10 - 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 7 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 6 * 7\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 84 / 2\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 17 % 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 2 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 + 4 * 2\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 11 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 20 - 5 - 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 12 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_PARENTHESES_45_GROUPING}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_PARENTHESES_45_GROUPING}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.3 Parentheses and Grouping\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Parentheses create a empty context. This allows prefix forms inside an otherwise operator chain, and explicit grouping when needed.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 * (- 2)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -10 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 2 * (3 + 4)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 14 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 (2 + 3) * (4 + 1)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 25 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_IDENTIFIER_45_SHAPES}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_IDENTIFIER_45_SHAPES}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.4 Identifier Shapes\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Identifiers can have name shape (alphanumeric) or operator shape (symbols). The shape is purely lexical and does not determine behavior. Whether an identifier acts as a prefix function or chain operator depends on its declaration and the register state.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 10 div 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 abs (- 5)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_LET_45_BINDINGS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_LET_45_BINDINGS}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.5 Let Bindings\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Let bindings introduce local variables. The syntax is let followed by a name and a value expression (no equals sign). Multiple statements are separated by colons or newlines.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl257 \fs19\f2 let x 5\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
