22\lang1033\f0 Relational operators compare the ordering of values.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 < 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 < 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 > 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 > 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 <= 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 <= 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 >= 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 >= 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_category_45_BOOLEAN_45_OPERATORS}{\*\bkmkend ID_category_45_BOOLEAN_45_OPERATORS}\b\fs31\f1 7.5 Boolean Operators\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Boolean operators combine boolean values.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_BOOLEAN_45_NEGATION}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_BOOLEAN_45_NEGATION}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 7.5.1 Boolean Negation\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 The tilde operator negates a boolean value.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 ~true\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 ~false\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_BOOLEAN_45_AND_45_OR}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_BOOLEAN_45_AND_45_OR}\b\fs28\f1 7.5.2 Boolean And/Or\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 The ampersand operator performs logical AND, the pipe operator performs logical OR.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true & true\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true & false\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false | false\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 false \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true | false\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 true \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_category_45_BITWISE_45_OPERATORS}{\*\bkmkend ID_category_45_BITWISE_45_OPERATORS}\b\fs31\f1 7.6 Bitwise Operators\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Bitwise operators manipulate integer values at the bit level.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_BIT_45_SHIFTS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_BIT_45_SHIFTS}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 7.6.1 Bit Shifts\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 The left shift operator shifts bits to the left, effectively multiplying by powers of two. The right shift operator shifts bits to the right, effectively dividing by powers of two.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 1 << 4\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 16 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 << 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 40 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 16 >> 2\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 4 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 100 >> 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 12 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_category_45_LAMBDAS}{\*\bkmkend ID_category_45_LAMBDAS}\b\fs31\f1 7.7 Lambdas\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 A lambda is an anonymous function written with a backslash: `\\params: body`. Parameters are space-separated. A lambda bound to a name and applied to arguments is monomorphized at the call site for those argument types, so the same lambda works at any argument type.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_LAMBDA_45_APPLICATION}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_LAMBDA_45_APPLICATION}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 7.7.1 Lambda Application\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 A lambda bound to a name can be called like a function.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl257 \fs19\f2 let inc \\x: x + 1\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
