unwrap(Option[int].Some(42))\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_GENERIC_45_OPTION}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_GENERIC_45_OPTION}\b\fs28\f1 7.11.3 Generic Option Types\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Generic unions like Option[T] work with choose for pattern matching.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl257 \fs19\f2 define Option[T] union: (Some: T, None)\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
