    print("glob works")\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\sl286 \fs22\lang1033\f0 Globs are convenient for a module whose types are used pervasively. Prefer single-type imports when a file uses only one or two names from a module \'97 they document the dependency more precisely.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_mod_45_use_45_diagnostic}{\*\bkmkend ID_mod_45_use_45_diagnostic}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 8.4.4 When a Type Is Not Visible\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Referencing a type that exists in the program but has not been imported fails the compile. The error names the module that defines the type and states the exact \f2 use\f0  line that would import it:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\sl257 \fs19\lang1024\f2 myprog.scaly:3:7: error: function not found: Box - defined in\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
